Id: stor009i
Severity: INFO
Category: filesystem
Check: check_storage
Fix: Reinstall onto LUKS, or convert in place with cryptsetup reencrypt.
References: crypttab(5), cryptsetup(8)
Controls: CIS 3.11; NIST SC-28; ISO 8.24

Auditing a system that is not running (tigris --root), its disk
encryption is read from what it sets up at boot: /etc/crypttab, which
names the encrypted devices it unlocks. This one names none, and its
/etc/fstab mounts a root file system, so unless the disks are encrypted
some other way (ZFS's native encryption, a self-encrypting drive, an
encrypted volume the hypervisor provides), whoever has them has the
data. The running system's check (stor004w, stor005i) looks at the
devices themselves; an image has only its configuration to go by.

Encrypting means reinstalling onto LUKS, which every installer offers,
or converting in place with cryptsetup reencrypt, after a backup.
